ion  with the scientific observation  and we had two uh five possibilities  the fingerprints dna digital aura voice  recognition and  face recognition and we know  fingerprints and dna  are the strongest one so we are looking  for possibilities  to do an investigation and an  identification  within  two or three hours and this was possible  and i will focus now on dna because  uh that was the most important uh  investigation for us in real time  identification  just to look back and i think until now  still in the netherlands  we work on this way we find  samples on the crime scene dna  fingerprints other samples  and then we're working working working  sometimes  hours uh it could be the whole day  and then we pack the samples we certify  the samples we bring it to a van and it  will transport it to a laboratory  our forensics laboratory in the region  then they will investigate it and pack  it  make a registration and do a second  investigation  maybe they found blood take a swipe of  blood and then they bring it to our  national forensic institute  where they only do the dna  investigations  they will start an investigation but  this will take a long time when you do  it very quickly maybe one day  when you're lucky but normally it will  take  days weeks and even months and that's  really true  so we had to speed up this process and  and  our idea was to not only the id  we're working now at the possibility to  do an investigation at the crime scene  so we put a rapid hit but also for  fingerprints and everything else  we put the equipment in a van  and we could do the analyze uh  now at a crime scene so  when you find uh maybe stabbing  find blood take a sample put it uh  in in your rapid hit  and uh you will see it we sent it to a  laboratory to the  to the database and they compare it  this could be done in in two hours  so when you're lucky you know the right  identity  uh maybe of the perpetrator or  somebody else within two or three hours  and that was the 